<p><em>"Every callback function should be memoized to prevent useless re-re=
ndering of child components that use the callback function"</em> is the rea=
soning of his teammates.</p>
<p>This reasoning is far from the truth. Such usage of <code>useCallback()<=
/code> without profiling makes the component slower and increases code comp=
lexity.</p>
<p>In this post, I'm going to explain how to use correctly <code>useCallbac=
k()</code>.</p>
