) accepts a function object as prop</a></li>
<li>When the function object is a dependency to other hooks, e.g. <code>use=
Effect(..., [callback])</code></li>
<li>When the function has some internal state, e.g. when the <a href=3D"htt=
ps://dmitripavlutin.com/react-throttle-debounce/#2-debouncing-a-callback-th=
e-first-attempt">function is debounced or throttled</a>.</li>
</ol>
