<p>The first problem is that <code>useCallback()</code> hook is called ever=
y time <code>MyComponent</code> renders. This already reduces the render pe=
rformance.</p>
<p>The second problem is that using <code>useCallback()</code> increases th=
e complexity of the code. You have to keep the <code>deps</code> of <code>u=
seCallback(..., deps)</code> in sync with what you're using inside the memo=
ized callback.</p>
<p>Does it worth using <code>useCallback()</code>? Most likely not because =
<code>&lt;MyChild&gt;</code> component is light, and its re-rendering doesn=
't create performance issues. <em>The optimization costs more than not havi=
ng the optimization</em>.</p>
