<h2 id=3D"5-summary" style=3D"position:relative"><a href=3D"https://dmitrip=
avlutin.com/react-usecallback/#5-summary" aria-label=3D"5 summary permalink=
" class=3D"anchor before"><span></span></a>5. Summary</h2>
<p>When thinking about performance tweaks, recall the <a href=3D"https://wi=
ki.c2.com/?ProfileBeforeOptimizing" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noref=
errer">statement</a>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Profile before optimizing</p>
</blockquote>
<p>When deciding to use an optimization technique, such as memoization with=
 <code>useCallback()</code>, do:</p>
<ol>
<li><a href=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/evaluate-performa=
nce/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Profile</a></li>
<li>Quantify the increased performance (e.g. <code>150ms</code> vs <code>50=
ms</code> render speed increase)</li>
<li>Ask yourself: does the increased performance, compared to increased com=
plexity, worth using <code>useCallback()</code>?</li>
</ol>
<p>To enable the memoization of the entire component output I recommend che=
cking my post <a href=3D"https://dmitripavlutin.com/use-react-memo-wisely/"=
>Use React.memo() wisely</a>.</p>
<p><em>Do you know use cases that are worth using <code>useCallback()</code=
>? Please share your experience in a comment below.</em></p></div><div clas=
